PAGES = {
    'index': {"title": 'Marcells Paper & Metal | Recovered paper and metal programs, nationwide', "desc": 'Chicago-based, family-owned since 1979. Mill-direct pricing, equipment financed within your program, and a live portal showing every load and statement. Programs nationwide, domestic and export mills.', "body": '<div class="hero">\n  <img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-hero.jpg" alt="">\n  <div class="shade"></div>\n  <div class="wrap">\n    <div class="kick"><i></i>Mill-direct &nbsp;·&nbsp; Equipment financed &nbsp;·&nbsp; Live portal</div>\n    <h1>Recovered paper and metal programs, run properly.</h1>\n    <p class="sub">We buy recovered paper, metal and plastics from printers, converters, manufacturers and distribution centers — one plant or forty. Pallets too: we build, repair, recycle and sell them. Mill-direct pricing, the equipment to make your material worth more, and a live portal showing every load and every statement.</p>\n    <div class="ctas"><a class="btn light" href="contact.html">Start a conversation</a><a class="btn ghost" href="programs.html">See how a program works →</a></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class="proof"><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="t"><div class="n">Since 1979</div><div class="l">family-owned, same phone number, same name on the door</div></div>\n  <div class="t"><div class="n">National</div><div class="l">service in every state, plus export to overseas mills</div></div>\n  <div class="t"><div class="n">Every load</div><div class="l">visible in your portal — scheduled, shipped, paid — with net weight and value</div></div>\n  <div class="t"><div class="n">6 days</div><div class="l">a week, Sunday pickups on request, special pickups dispatched within 24 hours</div></div>\n</div></div>\n\n<section><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="eyebrow">Why programs move to Marcells</div>\n  <h2 style="max-width:720px">Three things you won\'t get from a broker.</h2>\n  <div class="values">\n    <div class="val"><div class="img"><img src="assets/mpm2-bales.jpg" alt=""></div><div class="b"><div class="num">01 — Pricing</div><h3>Mill-direct, and you can see it</h3><p>Direct relationships with domestic and export mills. You see what your material earned and what moved the number — on a statement every month, not netted into a quarterly true-up you can\'t audit.</p><a class="more" href="programs.html">How pricing shows up →</a></div></div>\n    <div class="val"><div class="img"><img src="assets/mpm2-conveyor.jpg" alt=""></div><div class="b"><div class="num">02 — Equipment</div><h3>We finance the equipment</h3><p>Balers, conveyors, cart tippers, roll cutters. Sized to your tonnage and supported by us — and for sites with the right volume and deal structure, we finance it inside the program. Loose material on trucks is what costs you money; the equipment is how that stops.</p><a class="more" href="equipment.html">Equipment →</a></div></div>\n    <div class="val"><div class="img" style="background:var(--green);display:grid;place-items:center;padding:22px">\n      <div class="ui" style="width:100%;box-shadow:none"><div class="bar"><b>YOUR PROGRAM</b><span>Updated as loads ship</span></div><table><tr><th>Load</th><th>Grade</th><th class="r">Net lb</th><th class="r">Status</th></tr><tr><td>84 971</td><td>OCC</td><td class="r">41,880</td><td class="r"><span class="pill g">Paid</span></td></tr><tr><td>84 990</td><td>SOP</td><td class="r">39,120</td><td class="r"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span></td></tr><tr><td>85 004</td><td>Mixed</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r"><span class="pill k">Scheduled</span></td></tr></table></div>\n    </div><div class="b"><div class="num">03 — Visibility</div><h3>Your own portal</h3><p>Live pricing by grade, every load with weights and values, monthly statements, payment status and your recycling impact. Your login, updated as loads ship.</p><a class="more" href="portal.html">See the portal →</a></div></div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n\n<div class="band"><section><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="eyebrow">What we take</div>\n  <h2>Paper, metal, plastics, pallets. One pickup, one program.</h2>\n  <div class="svc">\n    <a href="paper.html"><b>Paper</b><span>OCC, SOP, mixed, news, DLK, high grades, pulp — from printers, converters and distribution.</span><em>Paper →</em></a>\n    <a href="metal.html"><b>Metal</b><span>Aluminum plates, mixed metals and bulky items — we strip, load and haul.</span><em>Metal →</em></a>\n    <a href="plastics.html"><b>Plastics</b><span>Industrial scrap plastics — film, strapping, totes and production scrap — baled or contained.</span><em>Plastics →</em></a>\n    <a href="pallets.html"><b>Pallets</b><span>Marcells Pallet Inc builds, repairs, recycles and sells pallets — on the same pickup and the same invoice.</span><em>Pallets →</em></a>\n    <a href="secure-destruction.html"><b>Secure destruction</b><span>Isolated site, 24-hour video surveillance with remote viewing, pickup included.</span><em>Secure destruction →</em></a>\n  </div>\n</div></section></div>\n\n<div class="ops"><section><div class="wrap">\n  <div><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#9fc9a8">Operations</div><h2>Same-day on requests before 10:00 am. Never later than the next morning.</h2><p style="color:#b7c4ba;margin-top:16px;font-size:17px">Six days a week, Sunday on request, special pickups dispatched within 24 hours. Spotted trailers, owner-operators and third-party carriers coordinated between your sites and the mills.</p></div>\n  <div class="clock"><div><b>6 days</b><span>a week, Sunday on request</span></div><div><b>&lt; 24 hrs</b><span>special pickups dispatched</span></div><div><b>10:00 am</b><span>same-day cutoff</span></div><div><b>1 → 40+</b><span>sites on one program</span></div></div>\n</div></section></div>\n\n<section><div class="wrap split">\n  <img src="assets/mpm2-aisle.jpg" alt="">\n  <div><div class="eyebrow">Since 1979</div><h2>How it all started.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin-top:16px">Still family-owned. Still picking up the phone. Now running programs across multiple states with the equipment and reporting most competitors don\'t offer.</p><p style="margin-top:20px"><a class="btn ghost dark" href="about.html">Read the story →</a></p></div>\n</div></section>'},
    'programs': {"title": 'How a Marcells program works | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'From one plant to a national footprint: we look at what you ship, fix the material, get the equipment in, and run one program across every site with monthly statements and a live portal.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:460px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-quonset.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:80px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Programs</div><h1>What a Marcells program looks like.</h1><p class="sub">From one plant to a national footprint — same grades, same reporting, same people.</p></div></div>\n\n<section><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="steps">\n    <div class="step"><div class="k">01</div><div><h3>We start by looking at what you\'re actually shipping.</h3><p>Load weights, grades, how many trucks a month, what\'s going out loose. Most sites are paying to move air.</p></div><img src="assets/mpm2-gaylord.jpg" alt=""></div>\n    <div class="step"><div class="k">02</div><div><h3>We fix the material before we fix the price.</h3><p>Baled beats loose by a wide margin — heavier loads, fewer trucks, better grade. If equipment is what\'s standing in the way, that\'s our problem to solve.</p></div><img src="assets/mpm2-bales2.jpg" alt=""></div>\n    <div class="step"><div class="k">03</div><div><h3>We get the equipment in.</h3><p>Balers, conveyors, cart tippers, roll cutters — sized to your tonnage. At the right volume and deal structure we finance it within the program, so the site pays nothing up front.</p></div><img src="assets/mpm2-conveyor.jpg" alt=""></div>\n    <div class="step"><div class="k">04</div><div><h3>One program across every site.</h3><p>Same grades, same reporting, same contacts, whether that\'s one plant or forty. We coordinate spotted trailers, owner-operators and third-party carriers between sites and mills.</p></div><img src="assets/mpm2-collapsible.jpg" alt=""></div>\n    <div class="step"><div class="k">05</div><div><h3>You see everything.</h3><p>Monthly statements per site, and a portal that updates as loads ship — pricing, loads, payments, impact.</p></div><div class="ui"><div class="bar"><b>STATEMENT — SITE 12</b><span>Sept 2026</span></div><div class="stmt"><div class="row"><span>Loads shipped</span><b>14</b></div><div class="row"><span>Net tons</span><b>268.4</b></div><div class="row"><span>Value</span><b class="blur">$48,210.00</b></div><div class="row tot"><span>Balance</span><b class="blur">$12,480.00</b></div></div><div class="foot">Sample data — illustrative</div></div></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class="callout"><div><h3>Multi-site is the normal case, not the exception.</h3><ul><li>Programs running across multiple states from one Chicago operations desk</li><li>Spotted trailers, owner-operators and third-party carriers between sites and mills</li><li>One set of grades, one reporting format, one phone number</li><li>Anonymised examples on request — we don\'t publish customer names</li></ul></div><div style="text-align:center"><a class="btn" href="contact.html">Have us look at your loads</a><p class="muted" style="margin-top:12px;font-size:13px">or call (773) 265-1200</p></div></div>\n</div></section>'},
    'portal': {"title": 'Customer portal | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Every MPM customer gets a login: pricing by grade, every load with weights and values, monthly statements, payments and recycling impact — updated as loads ship.', "body": '<div class="pdark">\n <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:84px;padding-bottom:0">\n  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#9fc9a8">The portal</div>\n  <h1 style="max-width:820px;color:#fff">Your program, visible.</h1>\n  <p class="lead" style="color:#c9d6cb;max-width:680px;margin-top:18px">Every customer gets a login. Pricing, loads, statements, payments and impact — updated as loads ship, not assembled when you ask.</p>\n  <p style="margin:26px 0 0"><a class="btn light" href="https://portals.cietrade.com/MarcellsPaperPortal/login.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Client Login</a> &nbsp; <a class="btn ghost" href="contact.html">Ask for a walkthrough</a></p>\n </div>\n <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:48px;padding-bottom:0;position:relative;z-index:2">\n  <div class="app">\n   <div class="app-chrome"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="url">MPM customer portal</span><span class="live"><i></i>Live · updated as loads ship</span></div>\n   <div class="app-body">\n    <aside class="app-side">\n      <div class="who"><b>Your company</b><span>All sites ▾</span></div>\n      <a href="#" class="on" data-t="overview">Overview</a><a href="#" data-t="pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#" data-t="loads">Loads</a><a href="#" data-t="statements">Statements</a><a href="#" data-t="payments">Payments</a><a href="#" data-t="impact">Impact</a><a href="#" data-t="bols">Documents</a>\n      <div class="side-foot">Sample data — illustrative.<br>Real figures shown to logged-in customers only.</div>\n    </aside>\n    <main class="app-main">\n     <div class="app-top"><b id="app-title">Overview</b><span>September 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 3 sites</span></div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel on" data-t="overview">\n      <div class="kpis">\n        <div><span>Loads this month</span><b>14</b><em>+3 vs Aug</em></div>\n        <div><span>Net tons</span><b>268.4</b><em>+11%</em></div>\n        <div><span>Value this month</span><b class="blur">$48,210</b><em class="blur">+$4,100</em></div>\n        <div><span>Next payment</span><b>Sep 30</b><em>ACH · scheduled</em></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class="charts">\n        <div class="chart"><div class="ch">Tons shipped by month</div><div class="cv"><canvas id="c-tons"></canvas></div></div>\n        <div class="chart"><div class="ch">Your price vs. published index — OCC</div><div class="cv"><canvas id="c-price"></canvas></div><div class="cf">Axis hidden on the public site. Your login shows the numbers.</div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class="recent"><div class="ch">Recent activity</div>\n        <div class="act"><span class="pill g">Paid</span><span>ACH cleared for August statement, Site 07</span><em>Sep 15</em></div>\n        <div class="act"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span><span>Ticket 51 633 · SOP · 38,760 lb · Site 12</span><em>Sep 19</em></div>\n        <div class="act"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span><span>Ticket 51 641 · Mixed · 40,010 lb · Site 03</span><em>Sep 22</em></div>\n        <div class="act"><span class="pill k">Scheduled</span><span>OCC pickup · Site 07 · trailer spotted</span><em>Sep 24</em></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="pricing">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Current pricing by grade</h3><span>Per net ton · updated monthly</span></div>\n      <table class="tbl"><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Basis</th><th class="r">Sept price</th><th class="r">vs Aug</th><th class="r">Trend</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>OCC</b></td><td>Index-linked</td><td class="r blur">$118.00</td><td class="r up">▲ <span class="blur">$6</span></td><td class="r"><span class="spark s1"></span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>SOP</b></td><td>Index-linked</td><td class="r blur">$212.00</td><td class="r up">▲ <span class="blur">$4</span></td><td class="r"><span class="spark s2"></span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>Mixed paper</b></td><td>Index-linked</td><td class="r blur">$62.00</td><td class="r dn">▼ <span class="blur">$2</span></td><td class="r"><span class="spark s3"></span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>DLK</b></td><td>Index-linked</td><td class="r blur">$154.00</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r"><span class="spark s1"></span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>Hard white</b></td><td>Index-linked</td><td class="r blur">$390.00</td><td class="r up">▲ <span class="blur">$10</span></td><td class="r"><span class="spark s2"></span></td></tr></table>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="loads">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Loads — all sites</h3><span><span class="chip">Sept 2026</span><span class="chip">All grades</span><span class="chip">Export CSV ↓</span></span></div>\n      <table class="tbl"><tr><th>Date</th><th>Ticket</th><th>Site</th><th>Grade</th><th class="r">Net lb</th><th class="r">Value</th><th class="r">Status</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/18</td><td>51 628</td><td>07</td><td>OCC</td><td class="r">42,340</td><td class="r blur">$2,498</td><td class="r"><span class="pill g">Paid</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/19</td><td>51 633</td><td>12</td><td>SOP</td><td class="r">38,760</td><td class="r blur">$4,109</td><td class="r"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/22</td><td>51 641</td><td>03</td><td>Mixed</td><td class="r">40,010</td><td class="r blur">$1,240</td><td class="r"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/22</td><td>51 644</td><td>07</td><td>OCC</td><td class="r">44,120</td><td class="r blur">$2,603</td><td class="r"><span class="pill b">Shipped</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/24</td><td>—</td><td>07</td><td>OCC</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r"><span class="pill k">Scheduled</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/26</td><td>—</td><td>12</td><td>SOP</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r">—</td><td class="r"><span class="pill k">Scheduled</span></td></tr></table>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="statements">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Statements</h3><span>One per site, per month · PDF</span></div>\n      <div class="stg">\n        <div class="stc"><b>Site 07</b><span>Aug 2026</span><div class="row"><span>Loads (11)</span><i class="blur">$31,840</i></div><div class="row"><span>Payments</span><i class="blur">–$28,560</i></div><div class="row tot"><span>Balance</span><i class="blur">$12,490</i></div><a>Download PDF ↓</a></div>\n        <div class="stc"><b>Site 12</b><span>Aug 2026</span><div class="row"><span>Loads (9)</span><i class="blur">$24,110</i></div><div class="row"><span>Payments</span><i class="blur">–$24,110</i></div><div class="row tot"><span>Balance</span><i class="blur">$0</i></div><a>Download PDF ↓</a></div>\n        <div class="stc"><b>Site 03</b><span>Aug 2026</span><div class="row"><span>Loads (6)</span><i class="blur">$9,870</i></div><div class="row"><span>Payments</span><i class="blur">–$6,200</i></div><div class="row tot"><span>Balance</span><i class="blur">$3,670</i></div><a>Download PDF ↓</a></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="payments">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Payments</h3><span>Last 60 days</span></div>\n      <table class="tbl"><tr><th>Date</th><th>Reference</th><th>Covers</th><th class="r">Amount</th><th class="r">Status</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/15</td><td>ACH 2026-0915</td><td>Aug statement · Site 07</td><td class="r blur">$14,220</td><td class="r"><span class="pill g">Cleared</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>08/30</td><td>ACH 2026-0830</td><td>Jul statement · Site 12</td><td class="r blur">$11,980</td><td class="r"><span class="pill g">Cleared</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>09/30</td><td>Scheduled</td><td>Aug statement · Site 03</td><td class="r blur">$3,670</td><td class="r"><span class="pill k">Upcoming</span></td></tr></table>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="impact">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Recycling impact — year to date</h3><span><span class="chip">All sites</span><span class="chip">2026 YTD ▾</span><span class="chip">Export for ESG ↓</span></span></div>\n      <div class="ibanner"><img src="assets/mpm2-impact_trees.jpg" alt=""><div class="ish"></div>\n        <div class="ib"><div class="ie">What 3,184 tons of recovered paper did this year</div><div class="in">54,100 <small>trees</small></div><div class="it">left standing — the equivalent of about <b>135 acres</b> of forest, or 68 Chicago city blocks of canopy.</div></div>\n        <div class="ilive"><i></i>Updated as loads ship</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class="icards">\n        <div class="ic"><img src="assets/mpm2-impact_water.jpg" alt=""><div class="ish"></div><div class="ib"><div class="in">22.3M <small>gal</small></div><div class="il">water saved</div><div class="it">≈ 34 Olympic pools</div></div></div>\n        <div class="ic"><img src="assets/mpm2-impact_air.jpg" alt=""><div class="ish"></div><div class="ib"><div class="in">9,870 <small>t</small></div><div class="il">CO₂e avoided</div><div class="it">≈ 2,150 cars off the road for a year</div></div></div>\n        <div class="ic"><img src="assets/mpm2-impact_energy.jpg" alt=""><div class="ish"></div><div class="ib"><div class="in">12.9M <small>kWh</small></div><div class="il">energy saved</div><div class="it">≈ 1,200 homes powered for a year</div></div></div>\n        <div class="ic"><img src="assets/mpm2-impact_landfill.jpg" alt=""><div class="ish"></div><div class="ib"><div class="in">9,550 <small>yd³</small></div><div class="il">landfill space avoided</div><div class="it">≈ 3 football fields, 6 ft deep</div></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class="charts" style="margin-top:12px;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr">\n        <div class="chart"><div class="ch">Tons diverted by month — and what they added up to</div><div class="cv" style="height:170px"><canvas id="c-impact"></canvas></div></div>\n        <div class="chart"><div class="ch">Diversion by grade</div><div class="cv" style="height:170px"><canvas id="c-grade"></canvas></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class="isites">\n        <div><b>Site 07</b><span>1,410 t</span><i style="width:44%"></i></div>\n        <div><b>Site 12</b><span>1,120 t</span><i style="width:35%"></i></div>\n        <div><b>Site 03</b><span>654 t</span><i style="width:21%"></i></div>\n        <div class="ix">Per-site breakdown exports as a one-page PDF your sustainability team can attach to corporate reporting. Equivalents use published EPA WARM factors. <em>Sample data — illustrative.</em></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n\n     <div class="tpanel" data-t="bols">\n      <div class="phead"><h3>Documents</h3><span>MPM bill of lading and scale ticket for every load</span></div>\n      <table class="tbl"><tr><th>Ticket</th><th>Date</th><th>Site</th><th>Grade</th><th class="r">Net lb</th><th class="r">Document</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>51 628</td><td>09/18</td><td>07</td><td>OCC</td><td class="r">42,340</td><td class="r"><a class="lnk">MPM BOL ↓</a></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>51 633</td><td>09/19</td><td>12</td><td>SOP</td><td class="r">38,760</td><td class="r"><a class="lnk">MPM BOL ↓</a></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>51 641</td><td>09/22</td><td>03</td><td>Mixed</td><td class="r">40,010</td><td class="r"><a class="lnk">Scale ticket ↓</a></td></tr></table>\n     </div>\n    </main>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </div>\n</div>\n\n<section style="padding-top:56px"><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="feat3">\n    <div><div class="num">Updated as loads ship</div><h3>Not a monthly PDF you have to ask for.</h3><p>Every load posts to your login when it crosses our scale. Status moves from scheduled to shipped to paid without a phone call.</p></div>\n    <div><div class="num">Per site, per month</div><h3>Statements that drop into your close.</h3><p>One statement per site with a running balance, downloadable as a PDF. Payments tie back to the statement they cover.</p></div>\n    <div><div class="num">Exportable</div><h3>Impact numbers your sustainability team can use.</h3><p>Tons, trees, water and CO₂e by site and month, exported in a format that goes straight into corporate reporting.</p></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:36px;font-size:13px">All figures above are sample data for illustration. Dollar values are shown only to logged-in customers.</p>\n</div></section>\n<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.5.0/dist/chart.umd.js" integrity="sha384-iU8HYtnGQ8Cy4zl7gbNMOhsDTTKX02BTXptVP/vqAWIaTfM7isw76iyZCsjL2eVi" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>\n<script>\n// portal side tabs\nconst sideLinks=[...document.querySelectorAll(\'.app-side a\')];\nsideLinks.forEach(a=>a.onclick=(e)=>{e.preventDefault();sideLinks.forEach(x=>x.classList.remove(\'on\'));a.classList.add(\'on\');document.querySelectorAll(\'.tpanel\').forEach(p=>p.classList.toggle(\'on\',p.dataset.t===a.dataset.t));document.getElementById(\'app-title\').textContent=a.textContent.replace(\'&\',\'&\');if(a.dataset.t===\'impact\')makeGrade();});\nlet made=false, gradeMade=false;\nfunction makeCharts(){ if(made||!window.Chart) return; made=true;\n const grid={color:\'#243129\'}, tick={color:\'#9fb3a5\',font:{size:11}};\n new Chart(document.getElementById(\'c-tons\'),{type:\'bar\',data:{labels:[\'Oct\',\'Nov\',\'Dec\',\'Jan\',\'Feb\',\'Mar\',\'Apr\',\'May\',\'Jun\',\'Jul\',\'Aug\',\'Sep\'],datasets:[{data:[212,198,231,205,220,244,238,251,262,240,242,268],backgroundColor:(c)=>c.dataIndex===11?\'#7fe08f\':\'#2f5a3f\',borderRadius:4}]},options:{responsive:true,maintainAspectRatio:false,plugins:{legend:{display:false},tooltip:{enabled:false}},scales:{x:{grid:{display:false},ticks:tick},y:{grid:grid,ticks:tick,border:{display:false}}}}});\n new Chart(document.getElementById(\'c-price\'),{type:\'line\',data:{labels:[\'Oct\',\'Nov\',\'Dec\',\'Jan\',\'Feb\',\'Mar\',\'Apr\',\'May\',\'Jun\',\'Jul\',\'Aug\',\'Sep\'],datasets:[{label:\'Your price\',data:[100,102,101,104,106,109,108,111,113,115,116,118],borderColor:\'#7fe08f\',backgroundColor:\'rgba(127,224,143,.12)\',fill:true,tension:.35,pointRadius:0,borderWidth:2},{label:\'Published index\',data:[90,91,90,93,94,96,96,98,100,101,102,104],borderColor:\'#c9a97c\',borderDash:[5,4],tension:.35,pointRadius:0,borderWidth:1.5}]},options:{responsive:true,maintainAspectRatio:false,plugins:{legend:{labels:{color:\'#c9d6cb\',boxWidth:10,font:{size:11}}},tooltip:{enabled:false}},scales:{x:{grid:{display:false},ticks:tick},y:{display:false}}}});\n}\nfunction makeGrade(){ if(gradeMade||!window.Chart) return; gradeMade=true;\n new Chart(document.getElementById(\'c-impact\'),{type:\'bar\',data:{labels:[\'Jan\',\'Feb\',\'Mar\',\'Apr\',\'May\',\'Jun\',\'Jul\',\'Aug\',\'Sep\'],datasets:[{data:[205,220,244,238,251,262,240,242,268],backgroundColor:\'#2f5a3f\',borderRadius:4,order:2},{type:\'line\',data:[205,425,669,907,1158,1420,1660,1902,2170],borderColor:\'#7fe08f\',pointRadius:0,borderWidth:2,tension:.3,yAxisID:\'y2\',order:1}]},options:{responsive:true,maintainAspectRatio:false,plugins:{legend:{display:false},tooltip:{enabled:false}},scales:{x:{grid:{display:false},ticks:{color:\'#9fb3a5\',font:{size:11}}},y:{grid:{color:\'#243129\'},ticks:{color:\'#9fb3a5\',font:{size:11}},border:{display:false}},y2:{position:\'right\',grid:{display:false},ticks:{color:\'#7fe08f\',font:{size:11}},border:{display:false}}}}});\n new Chart(document.getElementById(\'c-grade\'),{type:\'doughnut\',data:{labels:[\'OCC\',\'SOP\',\'Mixed\',\'DLK\',\'Hard white\'],datasets:[{data:[46,24,14,10,6],backgroundColor:[\'#2f5a3f\',\'#7fe08f\',\'#c9a97c\',\'#4f7a5c\',\'#e8d9bf\'],borderColor:\'#161d19\',borderWidth:2}]},options:{responsive:true,maintainAspectRatio:false,cutout:\'65%\',plugins:{legend:{position:\'right\',labels:{color:\'#c9d6cb\',boxWidth:10,font:{size:11}}},tooltip:{enabled:false}}}});\n}\nwindow.addEventListener(\'load\',()=>{makeCharts();});\n</script>'},
    'equipment': {"title": 'Equipment | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Balers, conveyors, cart tippers and roll cutters sized to your tonnage — financed by MPM for sites with the right volume and deal structure. Containers from gaylords to spotted trailers.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:460px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-aisle.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:80px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Equipment</div><h1>The right equipment, financed within your program.</h1><p class="sub">Balers, conveyors, cart tippers and roll cutters — sized to your tonnage, supported by us, and for sites with the right volume and deal structure, financed by MPM so there\'s nothing up front.</p></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="eyebrow">What we install</div><h2>Sized to your tonnage, supported for the life of the program.</h2>\n  <div class="gal" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-conveyor.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Conveyors<span>Feed from the floor or the line straight into the baler</span></figcaption></figure>\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-rolls.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Roll cutters &amp; cart tippers<span>For converters and printers running rolls and trim</span></figcaption></figure>\n  </div>\n  <div class="two">\n    <div class="box"><h3>How it works</h3><ul><li>Site analysis based on the tonnage your facility actually produces</li><li>Equipment matched to that tonnage — not the biggest machine we can place</li><li>At the right volume and deal structure, MPM finances the equipment inside the program agreement</li><li>Training and ongoing support included; terms discussed site by site, never published</li></ul></div>\n    <div class="box"><h3>What makes a site a fit</h3><ul><li>Enough monthly volume for the equipment to pay for itself in the material</li><li>A program term agreement so both sides can plan</li><li>No loose material on trucks — baled or contained, every load</li><li>Access to weights and grades so the reporting is real</li></ul></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:64px">Containers</div><h2>Gaylords, tubs, collapsibles, bins, spotted trailers.</h2>\n  <div class="gal" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-gaylord.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Gaylord boxes</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-tubs.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Plastic tubs</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-collapsible.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Collapsible containers</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure><img src="assets/mpm2-bins.jpg" alt=""><figcaption>Bin receptacles</figcaption></figure>\n  </div>\n</div></section>'},
    'coverage': {"title": 'Coverage | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Headquartered in Chicago, programs in every state, material shipped to domestic and export mills.', "body": '<section><div class="wrap split">\n  <div><div class="eyebrow">Coverage</div><h1 style="font-size:46px;color:var(--green)">Where we run: everywhere.</h1><p class="lead" style="margin-top:18px">Headquartered in Chicago at 4221 W Ferdinand. Programs across the whole country, coordinated from one operations desk — and material shipped wherever it earns the most, including export mills overseas.</p>\n  <div class="covs">\n    <div><b>All 48 contiguous states</b><span>Pickups, spotted trailers and program sites coast to coast</span></div>\n    <div><b>Domestic mills</b><span>Direct relationships, not a broker between you and the buyer</span></div>\n    <div><b>Export</b><span>Containerized loads to overseas mills when that\'s the best home for your grade</span></div>\n    <div><b>One desk</b><span>Same contacts, same reporting, whether the site is in Chicago or on the coast</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <p style="margin-top:26px"><a class="btn" href="contact.html">Ask about your region</a> &nbsp; <span class="muted" style="font-size:14px">or call (773) 265-1200</span></p></div>\n  <div>\n    <div class="map">\n      <i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="on">ME</i>\n      <i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="on">VT</i><i class="on">NH</i>\n      <i class="on">WA</i><i class="on">ID</i><i class="on">MT</i><i class="on">ND</i><i class="on">MN</i><i class="on">WI</i><i class="on">MI</i><i class="x"></i><i class="on">NY</i><i class="on">MA</i><i class="on">RI</i>\n      <i class="on">OR</i><i class="on">NV</i><i class="on">WY</i><i class="on">SD</i><i class="on">IA</i><i class="hq">IL</i><i class="on">IN</i><i class="on">OH</i><i class="on">PA</i><i class="on">NJ</i><i class="on">CT</i>\n      <i class="on">CA</i><i class="on">UT</i><i class="on">CO</i><i class="on">NE</i><i class="on">MO</i><i class="on">KY</i><i class="on">WV</i><i class="on">VA</i><i class="on">MD</i><i class="on">DE</i><i class="x"></i>\n      <i class="x"></i><i class="on">AZ</i><i class="on">NM</i><i class="on">KS</i><i class="on">AR</i><i class="on">TN</i><i class="on">NC</i><i class="on">SC</i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i>\n      <i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="on">TX</i><i class="on">OK</i><i class="on">LA</i><i class="on">MS</i><i class="on">AL</i><i class="on">GA</i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i>\n      <i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="on">FL</i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i><i class="x"></i>\n    </div>\n    <div class="exp"><span class="arr">←</span><b>Export</b> Pacific &amp; Atlantic ports → overseas mills <span class="arr">→</span></div>\n    <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:var(--green)"></i>Chicago headquarters</span><span><i style="background:var(--moss)"></i>Program coverage</span></div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>'},
    'about': {"title": 'About | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'How Scott Lowell turned a trunk of computer punch cards and a $1,000 loan into Marcells Paper & Metal, family-owned since 1979.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:420px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-aisle.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:80px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">About</div><h1>It started with punch cards.</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="story">\n  <p class="drop">Back in the mid to late 70’s, Scott Lowell was your average college student. One of the classes he was taking at the time was Statistics 101. On his way to this particular class, he would pass a room designated for computers only. In those days, the computer industry was just entering its humble beginnings and in order to communicate to computers, one would feed them punch-tab cards to deliver information. This process has since been modernized to what we now refer to as hard-drives on present day computers.</p>\n  <p>Scott noticed that the used key punch cards were being saved and placed back into the original boxes they came in. He got to talking with someone in the room who explained that a service comes in, buys the punch cards back and takes them away. He further learned that paper mills use the old key punch cards by recycling them into other paper products. He also found out that there were companies in the Chicago area that were also interested in buying them back. Scott discovered the name of such a company, called them up and asked them how much they were paying for scrap computer cards.</p>\n  <p>Scott soon realized that this could be a very good business prospect. He noticed that every Sunday when he opened up the job section of the paper, he would see between 300 and 400 want ads seeking computer analysts. Who better to have used computer cards than the companies searching for employees for their computers? Scott wanted to capitalize on the opportunity, but first he needed to do four things: develop a name for his company, open a checking account, get a truck to pick up the scrap computer cards, and find someone to sell them to.</p>\n  <p>Perhaps Scott’s biggest business feat to this day was obtaining the financing needed to purchase his first step van for pick-ups. Scott persuaded his grandmother to loan him $1,000 – which he paid back at $50 a month. At that time, Scott’s mother had a small dress shop located on Devon Avenue in Chicago. It was called “Marcells Custom Tailoring”. Scott explains that his mother always answered the phone the same way, “Marcells”. Marcells was the only word she ever said. Not “Marcells Custom Tailoring”, just “Marcells”. His mom said that she could take all of his calls too — and so the company got its name.</p>\n  <p>On off school days, holidays and such, Scott’s 12-year younger brother Jeff got involved, helping him out on the truck. Scott’s mother continued to answer his phone calls at her dress shop. Scott had business cards made up with the address and phone number of the dress shop. So when his mother answered the phones by saying “Marcells”, whether the caller was a customer of the dress shop or Scott’s paper recycling business in Chicago, IL, they had come to the right place!</p>\n</div>\n<div class="bridge"><h3>From one step van to nationwide programs.</h3><p>The business that started in 1979 with a borrowed $1,000 now runs recovered paper and metal programs across the country, ships to domestic and export mills, and gives every customer a live portal into their loads, statements and impact. Still family-owned. Still answering the phone.</p></div>\n</div></section>'},
    'paper': {"title": 'Paper recycling | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'All grades of recovered paper — OCC, DLK, ledger, news, high grades and pulp substitutes — bought mill-direct with containers and pickup from MPM.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:380px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-bales.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Materials</div><h1>Paper</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">\n<p>MPM buys recovered paper from printers, converters, manufacturers and distribution centers — a broad spectrum of grades from newspaper and corrugated to high grades and pulp substitutes. Our direct relationships with domestic and export mills let us work on your behalf and get the most out of every load.</p>\n<h2>Grades we buy</h2>\n<ul><li>Printers mix, sorted and mixed white ledger, colored ledger and envelope cuttings</li><li>Coated and uncoated book stock, news blanks and publication blanks</li><li>Old corrugated containers (OCC), double-lined kraft (DLK) and boxboard</li><li>Old newspaper, magazines and groundwood grades</li><li>Hard white, soft white and other pulp substitutes</li><li>Old inventory of paper — cut sheets and rolls</li></ul>\n<h2>What happens to your paper</h2>\n<p>Every load is weighed at our Chicago facility on a computerized scale system, graded, sorted to remove contaminants, and compacted into mill-specification bales. Our facility has immediate, adjacent rail service, so material moves to mills efficiently. Weights and values post to your portal login as loads cross the scale.</p>\n<h2>Containers and pickup</h2>\n<p>We supply what your site needs — gaylord boxes, plastic tubs, collapsible containers, bin receptacles or a spotted trailer — and schedule pickups around your production. Same-day service on requests before 10:00 am, six days a week, Sunday on request.</p>\n<p>Our sister company, <a href="pallets.html">Marcells Pallet Inc</a>, builds, repairs, recycles and sells pallets for the same customers — one pickup, one invoice, paper and pallets together.</p>\n<p><strong>Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a> or <a href="contact.html">tell us what you\'re shipping</a>.</strong></p>\n</div></div></section>'},
    'metal': {"title": 'Metal recycling | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Aluminum printing plates, mixed metals and bulky items collected and recycled by MPM with containers dropped at your facility.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:380px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-tubs-blue.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Materials</div><h1>Metal</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">\n<p>MPM isn\'t only paper. We collect and recycle metal waste from printers and manufacturers — aluminum printing plates above all, plus mixed metals and bulky items — with the equipment to strip, load and haul.</p>\n<h2>Why aluminum plates are worth recycling</h2>\n<p>Aluminum keeps its physical properties through recycling, so recycled and virgin aluminum are effectively the same material. Recycling plates reduces reliance on bauxite ore and uses a fraction of the energy of primary production — and it pays.</p>\n<h2>How it works</h2>\n<p>We drop containers of the right size at your facility, you fill them with plates and other metal (and paper), and we collect on a schedule that fits your production. Every load is weighed on our computerized scale and posted to your portal.</p>\n<h2>Construction and industrial metal</h2>\n<p>Any project produces metal waste that shouldn\'t go to a landfill and has to be handled correctly. We take care of collection and recycling so the material ends up where it should, with the paperwork to show it.</p>\n<p><strong>Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a> or <a href="contact.html">send us a message</a>.</strong></p>\n</div></div></section>'},
    'secure-destruction': {"title": 'Secure document destruction | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Discreet collection and destruction of sensitive documents at an isolated site inside the MPM facility under 24-hour video surveillance.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:380px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-bales2.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Materials</div><h1>Secure document destruction</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">\n<p>The secure destruction of sensitive documents and files is serious business, which is why MPM added a dedicated, isolated site inside our facility for exactly that purpose.</p>\n<h2>How it works</h2>\n<ul><li>Discreet collection of documents and files from your site, on a schedule or on request</li><li>Destruction at an isolated area of our facility used solely for this purpose</li><li>24-hour video surveillance with remote viewing access</li><li>Destroyed material is baled and recycled as paper — nothing goes to landfill</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a> to set up secure destruction for your office or plant.</strong></p>\n</div></div></section>'},
    'plastics': {"title": 'Plastics recycling | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Industrial scrap plastics — film, strapping, totes and production scrap — collected and recycled by MPM on the same program as your paper and metal.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:380px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-tubs.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Materials</div><h1>Plastics</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">\n<p>Alongside paper and metal, MPM buys industrial scrap plastics from the same plants — so one program and one pickup cover everything leaving your dock.</p>\n<h2>What we take</h2>\n<ul><li>Stretch film and shrink wrap</li><li>Plastic strapping</li><li>Totes, drums, crates and rigid containers</li><li>Production scrap and off-spec material</li></ul>\n<h2>How it works</h2>\n<p>Tell us what the material is and roughly how much you generate. We’ll set up the right container or baling approach, pick it up on your schedule, weigh it on our computerized scale and post it to your portal like any other load.</p>\n<p><strong>Not sure if we take it? Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a> — if it’s plastic and it’s industrial, we’ll tell you straight.</strong></p>\n</div></div></section>'},
    'pallets': {"title": 'Pallets | Marcells Pallet Inc', "desc": 'Marcells Pallet Inc builds, repairs, recycles and sells pallets — one pickup and one invoice alongside your paper, metal and plastics.', "body": '<div class="hero" style="min-height:380px"><img class="bg" src="assets/mpm2-collapsible.jpg" alt=""><div class="shade"></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#c9dccb">Marcells Pallet Inc</div><h1>Pallets</h1></div></div>\n<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">\n<p>Marcells Pallet Inc, our sister company, builds, repairs, recycles and sells pallets for the same customers MPM serves for paper, metal and plastics. One pickup, one invoice, everything together.</p>\n<h2>What we do</h2>\n<ul><li>Buy back and recycle your used and broken pallets</li><li>Repair and return pallets to service</li><li>Build new pallets to your spec</li><li>Sell new and recycled pallets by the truckload</li></ul>\n<h2>Why it works with a paper program</h2>\n<p>Pallets leave your building on the same trucks as your paper and metal. Putting them on the same program means fewer vendors, fewer trucks and one statement to reconcile.</p>\n<p><strong>Need pallets, or need them gone? Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a>.</strong></p>\n</div></div></section>'},
    'faq': {"title": 'FAQ | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": 'Answers about coverage, pickups, containers, materials, pricing and the customer portal.', "body": '<section><div class="wrap"><div class="prose"><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does MPM service accounts outside of Illinois?</summary><p>Yes. MPM runs programs nationwide — every state — and ships to domestic and export mills. See <a href="coverage.html">Coverage</a>.</p></details><details><summary>How often do you pick up, and do you operate on weekends?</summary><p>MPM operates 6 days a week and can arrange Sunday pickups on request. Special pickups can be dispatched within 24 hours by our customer service team, and same-day service is available on requests placed before 10:00 am.</p></details><details><summary>Do you supply the containers for my material?</summary><p>Yes. MPM provides a full range of containers, from gaylord boxes and collapsible containers to plastic tubs, bin receptacles and spotted trailers dropped at your facility. See <a href="equipment.html">Equipment</a>.</p></details><details><summary>What types of materials do you take?</summary><p>All grades of paper, aluminum plates and mixed metals, industrial scrap plastics, pallets, and secure-destruction documents.</p></details><details><summary>Does MPM buy old paper inventory?</summary><p>Yes. MPM buys old inventory in both cut sheets and rolls.</p></details><details><summary>How does MPM provide consistent pricing when the market is always changing?</summary><p>Our direct relationships with both domestic and international mills give us the flexibility to take advantage of movement and price.</p></details><details><summary>Will the price I receive fluctuate?</summary><p>Recovered paper is a commodity and pricing varies over time with the amount of material on the market. Your current price on every grade is always visible in your portal login.</p></details><details><summary>Can I see my loads and statements?</summary><p>Every customer gets a login to the MPM portal: pricing by grade, every load with weights and values, monthly statements per site, payment status and recycling impact — updated as loads ship.</p></details></div><p style="margin-top:24px">Still have a question? Call <a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a> or <a href="contact.html">send us a message</a>.</p></div></div></section>'},
    'contact': {"title": 'Contact | Marcells Paper & Metal', "desc": "Call (773) 265-1200 or tell us how many sites you have and what you're shipping.", "body": '<section><div class="wrap">\n  <div class="eyebrow">Contact</div><h1 style="font-size:46px;color:var(--green)">Have us look at your loads.</h1>\n  <div class="cgrid">\n    <div><p class="lead">The fastest way is the phone.</p><div class="bigphone"><a href="tel:+17732651200">(773) 265-1200</a></div><p class="muted">Same-day service on requests before 10:00 am. Six days a week, Sunday on request.</p>\n      <div class="box" style="margin-top:28px"><h3>What to tell us</h3><ul><li>How many sites, and where</li><li>What you\'re shipping now — grades, loose or baled</li><li>Roughly how many trucks a month</li><li>Whether you have equipment on site today</li></ul></div>\n      <p style="margin-top:22px" class="muted">4221 W Ferdinand St, Chicago, IL 60624 · Fax (773) 265-1220 · <a href="mailto:info@marcellspaper.com">info@marcellspaper.com</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=4221+W+Ferdinand+St+Chicago+IL+60624" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get directions</a></p>\n      <p style="margin-top:14px" class="muted">Already a customer? <a href="https://portals.cietrade.com/MarcellsPaperPortal/login.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>Client Login</b></a></p></div>\n    <div class="form box"><form onsubmit="return sendMail(this)">\n      <label for="name">Name</label><input id="name" name="Name" required placeholder="Your name">\n      <label for="company">Company</label><input id="company" name="Company" placeholder="Company">\n      <label for="reach">Email or phone</label><input id="reach" name="Reach" required placeholder="How should we reach you?">\n      <label for="sites">Number of sites</label><select id="sites" name="Sites"><option>1</option><option>2–5</option><option>6–20</option><option>20+</option></select>\n      <label for="msg">What are you shipping now?</label><textarea id="msg" name="Message" rows="4" placeholder="Grades, loose or baled, trucks per month…"></textarea>\n      <p style="margin-top:18px"><button class="btn" type="submit">Send</button></p>\n      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">Opens a pre-filled email to info@marcellspaper.com from your mail app. Or just call — it\'s faster.</p>\n    </form>\n    <script>\n    function sendMail(f){var b=\'Name: \'+f.Name.value+\'\\nCompany: \'+f.Company.value+\'\\nContact: \'+f.Reach.value+\'\\nSites: \'+f.Sites.value+\'\\n\\n\'+f.Message.value;\n      window.location.href=\'mailto:info@marcellspaper.com?subject=\'+encodeURIComponent(\'Program inquiry - \'+f.Name.value)+\'&body=\'+encodeURIComponent(b);return false;}\n    </script></div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>'},
}
